From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [trainer] feat: grpo_length_penalty, GRPO on rewards that
 reinforce the shorter of two successes more

The estimator grpo_length_penalty shapes a success's reward, an exact reward of one, into max(1, L / L_min) ** -coeff:
L its generated tokens, L_min those of its group's shortest success and coeff algorithm.length_penalty_coeff, which
the estimator requires. A group with a failure is normalized as in GRPO; a group of successes, which differs by length
alone, is only centred on its mean. The v1 trainer computes it from each session's final output, as it does GRPO, and
DAPO keeps a group of successes whose generated tokens still set their advantages apart; it reads the response masks
of such groups alone.
